# {{FLEET_NAME}} — Canon Conventions

> The shared **canonical-data layer** of this fleet: the published business facts humans
> and agents rely on, plus the protocols that define how agents work together. This repo
> is the company's source of truth — versioned, reviewed, co-edited by humans and agents.
> Seeded by `/add-canon` on {{DATE}}; this file is live fleet configuration — edit via PR.

## Layout

```
CONVENTIONS.md      # this file — the rules of the layer
CODEOWNERS          # folder → responsible human counterpart (review routing)
agents/<name>/      # one folder per agent — that agent's published record, owned
protocols/          # inter-agent contracts — schemas, channels, cadences
```

## Ownership

- Every `agents/<name>/` folder has exactly **one owner** — the agent named `<name>`.
- The owner commits **directly** inside its own folder and carries the duty to keep it
  true (its `/canon-reconcile` pass verifies and stamps on a schedule).
- **Everyone else — agent or human — changes someone's folder or `protocols/` via
  branch + PR.** CODEOWNERS routes the review. No exceptions for trivial edits.
- **One sanctioned exception — enrollment seeding:** when an agent joins the canon
  (`/add-canon`, including its fleet-enrollment step), the installer may create that
  agent's `agents/<name>/` folder with its stub + CODEOWNERS line. Creation only —
  everything after belongs to the owner.
- Git history is the audit trail: no force-pushes, no history rewrites, ever.

## Canonical files

Published facts live in markdown (or YAML for structured data) with front-matter:

```yaml
---
owner: <agent-name>     # must match the enclosing agents/<name>/ folder
updated: YYYY-MM-DD     # last content change
verified: YYYY-MM-DD    # last time the owner confirmed it against its source
source: <where this fact comes from — a workspace path, an API, a doc, or "manual">
---
```

- **Staleness bound: 30 days.** Consumers flag anything whose `verified:` is older —
  stale canon is served with a warning, never as silently-current fact.
- Publish **facts, not working state**: if the rest of the fleet shouldn't depend on it,
  it belongs in the agent's private workspace, not here.
- **No secrets.** Credentials, tokens, and keys never land in this repo — the canon is
  public-safe by default.

## Protocols

A protocol is a contract two or more agents (or an agent and a human process) agree on:
message shape, channel, cadence, escalation. One file per protocol under `protocols/`,
same front-matter (owner = the proposing agent), changes via PR with every party's
owner as reviewer.

## Humans

Humans co-edit under the same rules: any folder via PR; direct pushes only where you are
the listed CODEOWNERS counterpart and the owning agent is informed (its next reconcile
will re-verify what changed).
